# ux-forces-full — the nine live-force knobs as studio controls: the studio's own floor plus the
# three browser gates the measurement doc quotes (docs/measurements/ux-forces-full.md).
#
# `expect` is `0` or `nonzero`; `#` starts a comment (scripts/orch/gate.sh:2-4). Every gate needs
# `scripts/studio.sh build` first, which the orchestrator runs before this file.
#
# KNOWN RED: `interact` fails on `int-node-drag` — the node lands 146.16 px from the pointer after
# a 150 px drag. The same row measures 145.89 px on origin/develop's own build
# (deploy/nav/interact.py over target/dist-before), so it is red before the knobs existed; the drag
# files (element.ts, motor/bridge.ts, motor/session.ts) belong to the open perf-pm-live branch.
# It is left in, not dropped: see docs/measurements/ux-forces-full.md.

studio-check|0|scripts/studio.sh check

# The live loop: settle, drag-neighbour, progress strip, dead worker — and its control.
live|0|scripts/studio-live.sh
negctl-live|nonzero|STUDIO_LIVE_BREAK=1 scripts/studio-live.sh

# Pointer interaction: hover, click, box select, node drag, node menu — and its control.
interact|0|scripts/studio-interact.sh
negctl-interact|nonzero|STUDIO_INTERACT_BREAK=1 scripts/studio-interact.sh

# The overlap probe: drawn discs covering each other after a settle at the defaults and after
# `forces.spread`, on the clustered fixture and a 10 000-node source, plus the live frame rate
# and the four fault channels. Its control skips `spread`, so its three `spread` rows are NOT-RUN.
overlap|0|scripts/studio-overlap.sh
negctl-overlap|nonzero|STUDIO_OVERLAP_BREAK=1 scripts/studio-overlap.sh